{
  "description": "How a node answers a client's frame. state \"new\": before hello; \"ready\": after welcome. Members a frame does not define are ignored. An auth frame needs id, key and sig (strings) and t (an integer); whether it checks is the auth area. A rank frame needs board, measure and division (strings); whether their values are allowed is answered bad_field, not a frame error (9.3). A nets frame needs keys (a list). board is no longer a message (version 1 replaced it with rank before any release). A state frame (5.11) carries rec (the live state, checked as the records area does with as: state) and may carry an id (then it is answered ack or err; without one only an err is sent). The measure now is a value of rank and rankwhy like the others; rankwhy may carry at, the time of the snapshot the ranking used.",
